<title>USA: CBOT March wheat falls to new contract low late.</title>
<headline>CBOT March wheat falls to new contract low late.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>CBOT March wheat dropped to a new contract low of $3.52-1/2 in late dealings when fund selling hit the market, traders said.</p>
<p>Sell stops were triggered when March broke support at $3.54-1/2 per bushel, its previous contract low which was set Friday.</p>
<p>At 1250 CST, wheat was 1-1/2 cents per bushel lower to 2-3/4 higher, with March down two at $3.54.</p>
<p>((Sam Nelson 312-408-8721))</p>
</text>
